import pytest

@pytest.fixture
def cart():
    return Cart(tax_rate=0.10)

def test_empty_cart_total_is_zero(cart):
    assert cart.total() == 0

def test_total_includes_tax(cart):
    cart.add(Item("book", price=20))
    assert cart.total() == pytest.approx(22)
```

A **fixture** is setup code that pytest injects by matching the **parameter name**. By default it runs again for each test, so each gets a fresh `cart`. Use `yield` instead of `return` to run cleanup after the test; put shared fixtures in `conftest.py`.

